Read section 5 if you only want to know the rule for forks.

1. Definitions

"You" means the person or organisation using the Software.
"Derivative" means any work that is based on the Software, including a modified
version, a port, a translation, a reimplementation of a substantial part of it,
or a work that incorporates a substantial part of it.
"Distribute" means to give, publish, upload, sell, sublicense, lend or otherwise
make the Software or a Derivative available to anyone other than You.
"Credit" means the notice described in section 5(b).

2. What You may do

a) Run the Software, free of charge, for personal or commercial work, on
   machines You own or control.
b) Make copies of the Software for backup, testing and archival purposes.
c) Read, study and learn from the source code if You lawfully receive it.

3. Conditions on every use

a) Keep every copyright, licence and attribution notice in the Software.
b) Do not remove, hide or alter the name "Lantas", the copyright line, or the
   links to the project.
c) Do not represent the Software as Your own work.

4. What You may not do without prior written permission

a) Distribute the Software, in whole or in part, in any form.
b) Distribute a Derivative, except as allowed by section 5.
c) Sell, rent, lease, sublicense or charge for the Software or a Derivative.
d) Make the Software or a Derivative available to others as a hosted or managed
   service, or bundle it into a product You offer.
e) Use the "Lantas" name, wordmark or logo for a fork, product or service, apart
   from the factual credit required by section 5.

5. Building on the Software: open source and credit

This is the only way a Derivative may be Distributed. If You create a Derivative
and Distribute it, then all of the following must be true:

a) The Derivative is licensed under this same licence, Lantas License 1.0, and
   carries a copy of it.
b) It gives clear Credit to the original in its about screen, its README and any
   website for it, worded at least as: "Based on Lantas, originally by Anwar
   Kalonov — https://github.com/AnwarKalonov", with the link visible and
   clickable wherever the credit appears in a user interface.
c) You publish the complete corresponding source code of the Derivative, under
   this licence, free of charge, at the same place the Derivative is published,
   in a form that can be rebuilt.
d) You do not charge for the Derivative, and You do not add technical measures
   that prevent recipients from exercising the rights in this licence.

Nothing in this section permits Distributing the unmodified Software, or a
Derivative that does not meet every condition above. A copy that fails these
conditions is not licensed, and section 7 applies.

